\
This dirge increases your health regeneration by %d.  The regeneration will increase with your level.", "tformat", true) -- 
tDef(95, "Dirge of Conquest", "talent name", true) -- 
tDef(147, "Sing a song of violence and victory (mostly violence) and sustain yourself through cruelty.\
Each time you deal a critical strike you gain 10%% of a turn (only once per turn).\
Each time you kill a creature you gain %d%% of a turn (only once per turn).\
", "tformat", true) -- 
tDef(155, "Dirge of Pestilence", "talent name", true) -- 
tDef(206, "Sing a song of decay and defiance and sustain yourself through spite.\
\9\9\9\9\9\9\9Each time you suffer a detrimental effect, you gain a shield with strength %d, that lasts as long as the effect would.  This will add to and extend an existing shield if possible.\
\9\9\9\9\9\9\9This can only trigger once every %d turns", "tformat", true) -- 
tDef(214, "Dirge Acolyte", "talent name", true) -- 
tDef(255, "Even now, something compels you to sing.\
\9\9\9Dirge of Famine: Increases health regen by %d.\
\9\9\9Dirge of Conquest: Gives you part of a turn on critical (10%%) or kill (%d%%).\
\9\9\9Dirge of Pestilence: Shields you for %d when an enemy inflicts a detrimental effect on you (5 turn cooldown).\
\9\9\9You may only have one Dirge active at a time.", "tformat", true) -- 
tDef(270, "Dirge Intoner", "talent name", true) -- 
tDef(280, "Your dirges carry the pain within you, which threatens to swallow those who come too close.  Anyone who hits you in melee suffers %0.2f mind damage.\
\9\9\9\9\9\9\9You, on the other hand, are steadied by the song.  Your dirges increase your resistance to stun and knockback by %d%%.\
\9\9\9\9\9\9\9The damage will increase with your Mindpower and your level.", "tformat", true) -- 
tDef(287, "Dirge Adept", "talent name", true) -- 
tDef(295, "Your dirges echo mournfully through the air.  When you end a dirge, you continue to gain its acolyte-level effects for %d turns.  You can only benefit from one such lingering dirge at a time.\
\
Furthermore, you are given focus by the song.  Your dirges increase your resistance to confusion and fear by %d%%.", "tformat", true) -- 
tDef(302, "Dirge Nihilist", "talent name", true) -- 
tDef(309, "Your dirges deaden you to the outside world, reducing all incoming damage by %d.\
The damage reduction will increase with your Spellpower.", "tformat", true) -- 


