tDef(83, "Attempt to finish off a wounded enemy, striking them with both weapons for %d%% increased by 50%% if their life is below 30%%.  A target brought below 20%% of its maximum life must make a physical save against your Accuracy or be instantly slain.\
\9\9You may take advantage of finishing your foe this way to activate stealth (if known).", "tformat", true) -- 
tDef(90, "Terrorize", "talent name", true) -- 
tDef(108, "When you exit stealth, you reveal yourself dramatically, intimidating foes around you. \
\9\9All foes within radius %d that witness you leaving stealth will be stricken with terror, which randomly inflicts stun, slow (40%% power), or confusion (50%% power) for %d turns.\
\9\9The chance to terrorize improves with your combat accuracy.", "tformat", true) -- 
tDef(116, "Garrote", "talent name", true) -- 
tDef(138, "#Target# avoids a garrote from #Source#!", "logCombat", true) -- 
tDef(149, "When attacking from stealth, you slip a garrote over the target’s neck (or other vulnerable part).  This strangles for %d turns and silences for %d turns.  Strangled targets are pinned and suffer an automatic unarmed attack for %d%% damage each turn. \
\9\9Your chance to apply the garrote increases with your Accuracy and you must stay adjacent to your target to maintain it.\
\9\9This talent has a cooldown.", "tformat", true) -- 
tDef(157, "Marked for Death", "talent name", true) -- 
tDef(190, "You mark a target for death for 4 turns, causing them to take %d%% increased damage from all sources. When this effect ends they will immediately take physical damage equal to %0.2f plus %d%% of all damage taken while marked.\
\9\9If a target dies while marked, the cooldown of this ability is reset and the cost refunded.\
\9\9This ability can be used without breaking stealth.\
\9\9The base damage dealt will increase with your Dexterity.", "tformat", true) -- 


