%s", "tformat", true) -- 
tDef(137, "Arcane Might", "talent name", true) -- 
tDef(140, "You have learned to harness your latent arcane powers, channeling them through your weapon.\
\9\9This has the following effects:\
\9\9Equipped weapons are treated as having an additional 50%% Magic modifier;\
\9\9Your raw Physical Power is increased by 100%% of your raw Spellpower;\
\9\9Your physical critical chance is increased by 25%% of your bonus spell critical chance.", "tformat", true) -- 
tDef(150, "Temporal Form", "talent name", true) -- 
tDef(152, "Have cast over 1000 spells and visited a zone outside of time", "_t", true) -- 
tDef(165, "You can wrap temporal threads around you, assuming the form of a telugoroth for 10 turns.\
\9\9While in this form you gain pinning, bleeding, blindness and stun immunity, 30%% temporal resistance, your temporal damage bonus is set to your current highest damage bonus + 30%%, 50%% of the damage you deal becomes temporal, and you gain 20%% temporal resistance penetration.\
\9\9You also are able to cast anomalies: Anomaly Rearrange, Anomaly Temporal Storm, Anomaly Flawed Design, Anomaly Gravity Pull and Anomaly Wormhole.", "tformat", true) -- 
tDef(173, "Blighted Summoning", "talent name", true) -- 
tDef(175, "Have summoned at least 100 creatures. More permanent summons may count as more than 1.", "_t", true) -- 
tDef(261, "You infuse blighted energies into all of your summons, granting them Bone Shield (level 3) and a bonus to Spellpower equal to your Magic.\
\9\9Your Wilder Summons and Necrotic Minions will gain special corrupted talents (level 3), other summons will gain 10%% Blight damage conversion and Virulent Disease (level 3).\
\9\9#GREEN#Wilder Summons:#LAST#\
\9\9- War Hound: Gnaw\
\9\9- Jelly: Curse of Defencelessness\
\9\9- Minotaur: Ruin\
\9\9- Golem: Acid Blood\
\9\9- Ritch: Life Tap\
\9\9- Hydra: Blood Spray\
\9\9- Rimebark: Poison Storm\
\9\9- Fire Drake: Flame of Urh’Rok\
\9\9- Turtle: Elemental Discord\
\9\9- Spider: Blood Grasp\
\9\9#GREY#Necrotic Minions:#LAST#\
\9\9- Skeleton Mages: Bone Spear\
\9\9- Skeleton Archers: Bone Spike\
\9\9- Skeleton Warriors: Ruin\
\9\9- Bone Giants: Bone Spike and Ruin\
\9\9- Ghouls: Virulent Disease\
\9\9- Dread: Slumber\
\9\9%s\
\9\9", "tformat", true) -- 
tDef(287, "Revisionist History", "talent name", true) -- 
tDef(293, "Have time-travelled at least once", "_t", true) -- 
tDef(310, "You can now control the recent past. Upon using this prodigy you gain a temporal effect for 20 turns.\
\9\9While this effect holds you can use the prodigy again to rewrite history.\
\9\9This prodigy splits the timeline. Attempting to use another spell that also splits the timeline while this effect is active will be unsuccessful.", "tformat", true) -- 
tDef(317, "Unfold History", "talent name", true) -- 
tDef(332, "Rewrite the recent past to go back to when you cast Revisionist History.", "tformat", true) -- 
tDef(338, "Cauterize", "talent name", true) -- 
tDef(341, "Have received at least 3500 fire damage and have cast at least 1000 spells", "_t", true) -- 
tDef(352, "Your inner flame is strong. Each time that you receive a blow that would kill you, your body is wreathed in flames.\
\9\9The flames will cauterize the wound, fully absorbing all damage done this turn, but they will continue to burn for 8 turns.\
\9\9Each turn 10%% of the damage absorbed will be dealt by the flames. This will bypass resistance and affinity.\
\9\9Warning: this has a cooldown.", "tformat", true) -- 
tDef(360, "Lich", "talent name", true) -- 
tDef(362, "Is a living creature that knows necromancy", "_t", true) -- 
tDef(367, "Have completed the ritual", "_t", true) -- 
tDef(433, "#GREY#As you turn into a powerful undead you feel your body violently rejecting the Blood of Life.", "log", true) -- 
tDef(439, "Lichform", "_t", true) -- 
tDef(439, "#GREY#You feel your life slip away, only to be replaced by pure arcane forces! Your flesh starts to rot on your bones, and your eyes fall apart as you are reborn into a Lich!\
\
#{italic}#You may now choose to customize the appearance of your Lich, this can not be changed afterwards.", "_t", true) -- 
tDef(440, "Lich Cosmetic Options", "_t", true) -- 
tDef(441, "Customize Appearance", "_t", true) -- 
tDef(441, "Use Default", "_t", true) -- 
tDef(443, "#GREY#You feel your life slip away, only to be replaced by pure arcane forces! Your flesh starts to rot on your bones, and your eyes fall apart as you are reborn into a Lich!", "_t", true) -- 
tDef(454, "#DARK_ORCHID#You are on your way to Lichdom. #{bold}#Your next death will finish the ritual.#{normal}#", "say", true) -- 
tDef(465, "This is your true goal and the purpose of all necromancy - to become a powerful and everliving Lich!\
\9\9Once learnt, the next time you are killed, the arcane forces you unleash will be able to rebuild your body into the desired Lichform.\
\9\9Liches are immune to poisons, diseases, fear, cuts, stuns, do not need to breath and are 20%% resistant to cold and darkness.\
\9\9Liches also gain +12 Magic, Willpower and Cunning, 60%% chance to ignore critical hits, +4 life rating (not retroactive), +35 spell and mental saves and 7 mana regeneration.\
\
\9\9Liches gain a new racial tree with the following talents:\
\9\9- Neverending Unlife: A Lich body is extremely resilient, being able to go into negative life and when destroyed it can regenerate itself.\
\9\9- Frightening Presence: Your mere presence is enough to shatter the resolve of most, reducing their saves, damage and movement speed.\
\9\9- Doomed for Eternity: As a creature of doom and despair you now constantly spawn undead shadows around you.\
\9\9- Commander of the Dead: You are able to infuse all undead party members (including yourself) with un-natural power, increasing your physical and spellpower.\
\9\9", "tformat", true) -- 
tDef(480, "High Thaumaturgist", "talent name", true) -- 
tDef(483, "Unlocked the High Thaumaturgist evolution", "_t", true) -- 
tDef(496, "High Thaumaturgist", "_t", true) -- 
tDef(501, "Thaumaturgists have unlocked a deeper understanding of their spells, allowing them to combine the elements into new ways and to empower them.\
\9\9The spells Flame, Manathrust, Lightning, Pulverizing Auger and Ice Shards are permanently turned into 3-wide beams spells.\
\9\9In addition they have access to the unique Thaumaturgy class tree:\
\9\9- Orb of Thaumaturgy: a temporary orb that duplicates any beam spells that you cast\
\9\9- Multicaster: When casting a beam spell adds a chance to also cast an other archmage spell\
\9\9- Slipstream: Allows movement when casting beams\
\9\9- Elemental Array Burst: a powerful, multi-elemental beam spell that can inflict all elemental ailments and can not be resisted\
\9\9#CRIMSON#The fine spellcasting required for wide beams and all thaumaturgy spells can only happen while wearing cloth. Anything heavier will hinder the casting too much.", "tformat", true) -- 


